        "id": 1718464399,
        "content": "Interesting problem. I imagine that we need some type of special value to instruct to the parser to exclude it from the calculation entirely. Perhaps we can use `null` or even `ignore`?\r\nFor example:\r\n```\r\nul: 0\r\nli: 0.5\r\ni: ignore\r\n```\r\n```\r\n- this is a _test_\r\n```\r\nWould yield `0.5 + ( 0.1 * 3 ) = 0.8`, ignoring \"_test_\"",
